From 594f1dba280230cb91db527f89d4ac19a97dddbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:19:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] RISC OS: switches for map, terrain and town animations

Adventure Map options gain three switches: map object animations,
terrain animations (both existing settings) and a new town animation
setting, adventure.townAnimation, which keeps town buildings and the
creature pictures (creature windows, fort, blacksmith) on their first
frame. Less to draw on slower computers. The right-hand column is
spaced 25 pixels apart so all ten rows fit.
